#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# spherical_bessel_y

#% text
# `spherical_bessel_y(n, z)` gives the spherical Bessel function y_n(z).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Integer orders give elementary functions of sin(z) and cos(z); other numeric orders sqrt(pi/(2 z)) times the Bessel function of order n + 1/2.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
spherical_bessel_y(0, x)
#% output
#= -1*cos(x)/x

#% cell
spherical_bessel_y(1, x)
#% output
#= -1*cos(x)*x^-2 + -1/x*sin(x)

#% cell
spherical_bessel_y(2, 1.5)
#% output
#= -1.3457126936204509

